<title>RUSSIA: Russia Uralsvyazinform preliminary '96 net rises.</title>
<headline>Russia Uralsvyazinform preliminary '96 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>AO Uralsvyazinform (preliminary results):</p>
<p>     (billion roubles)			1996	1995</p>
<p>     pre-tax profit			   139.5	91.9</p>
<p>     net profit				 104.7	72.0</p>
<p>     gross income			     596.5     361.8</p>
<p>     sales (household)			163.8	84.8</p>
<p>     operating costs			  475.0     269.4</p>
<p>     profitability (percent)		 31.1	34.1</p>
<p>AO Uralsvyazinform is based in Perm, southern European Russia.</p>
<p>Accounts are to Russian standard, which is intended for tax calculation and not investment consideration. Equities analysts say Russian accounting standards differ widely from international standards and can be misleading as a representation of a company's financial worth.</p>
<p>				  1997E	1996	 1995</p>
<p>lines brought into service</p>
<p> Cities			 59,200     52,700     23,800</p>
<p> Rural areas		     400	  -	  3,000</p>
<p> Pagers			   -	   2,000	  -</p>
<p>Mobile phones to standard</p>
<p>  NMT-450			 -	   2,300	  -</p>
<p>  DAMPS-800		    1,200	3,800	  -</p>
<p>  GSM-900			5,200	  -	    -</p>
<p>The company said it expected 1997 turnover to be 990.1 billion roubles, including 386.1 billion roubles from local networks and 444.6 billion from its inter-city network.</p>
<p>--Olga Popova, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
